      "title": "Deep Imitation Learning for Humanoid Loco-manipulation Through Human Teleoperation",
      "takeaway": "TRILL addresses the difficulty of collecting demonstrations and training policies for high-degree-of-freedom humanoid loco-manipulation by pairing a VR interface for human demonstration collection with a whole-body control formulation that maps task-space operator commands to joint-torque actuation while stabilizing robot dynamics. The framework adds high-level action abstractions tailored to humanoid loco-manipulation so that complex sensorimotor skills can be learned data-efficiently through deep imitation learning. The abstract reports demonstrations of TRILL in simulation and on a real-world robot across various loco-manipulation tasks but gives no quantitative results. While reading, inspect how the action abstractions are defined and how the whole-body controller is coupled to the learned policy.",
